<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugenio Matte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Eugenio Matte Hurtado</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugenio Matte Hurtado (1895–1934) was a Chilean lawyer and socialist politician, grand master of the Grand Lodge of Chile. He took part in the coup of 4 June 1932 that created the Socialist Republic of Chile and sat on its governing junta until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-davila">Carlos Dávila</a> ousted him and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Marmaduke Grove</a> later that month and sent them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Easter Island</a>. In 1933 he helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-chile">Socialist Party of Chile</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eugenio-matte.jpg" alt="Eugenio Matte" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eugenio_Matte_Hurtado-Jornada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
